  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Wisconsin recorded $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2.1B, making the Department of Veterans Affairs the dominant buyer in the state so far this fiscal year. The federal award count in Wisconsin is 53,086 and the average award size is $55.1K. Obligations fell 53.3% year over year. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. received $1.9B in obligations, making OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. the largest vendor by dollars this year. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest industry by obligations at $1.8B. Truck Trailer Manufacturing and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing follow at $334M and $291M respectively. Historical annual obligations show fluctuations: FY21 was $5.8B, FY22 was $5.2B, FY23 was $5.3B, FY24 was $8.9B, and FY25 was $6.3B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most in Wisconsin this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2.1B in Wisconsin in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $481M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $171M. The Department of Justice, the Department of the Interior, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $47.2M, $38.2M, and $31M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and what industries get the most work?",
        "body": "OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. received $1.9B in obligations and OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC received $466M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) leads industries at $1.8B, followed by Truck Trailer Manufacturing at $334M and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $291M. Other notable vendors include AMTEC CORPORATION at $267M and GE PRECISION HEALTHCARE LLC at $127M."
      }
    ]
  },
